    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line via the logger named `AUDIT` containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` on successful create.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Logs to `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` with the owner's id, customerCode, and registrationDate.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` (so the owner already has its generated id) and `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the pipeline.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test \u2014 and the full suite \u2014 pass. The captured line confirms it: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-14`, whose id/customerCode/registrationDate the test matches against the values read back from `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
